 Recording Rules in Prometheus â Architecture and Performance Engineering
Objectives
Design and deploy a multi-group recording rule hierarchy that eliminates redundant query computation across dependent rule groups
Measure and quantify the latency difference between raw PromQL expressions and their precomputed recording rule equivalents under sustained load
Diagnose recording rule evaluation failures using Prometheus internal metrics and the rules API
Prerequisites
Comfort with Linux process management, systemd unit files, and file permission models
Familiarity with time series concepts: labels, cardinality, scrape intervals, and range vectors
Prior exposure to PromQL syntax including aggregation operators and rate functions
Lab Environment
You will work on a dedicated AWS EC2 Ubuntu instance provided by Al Nafi. The instance has a base Ubuntu installation; you will install all required tools in Task 1.

Task 1: Install and Verify the Observability Stack
