Step 1.2: Write a Minimal Prometheus Configuration and Verify Scraping
Write /etc/prometheus/prometheus.yml so that Prometheus scrapes itself and Node Exporter, and references a rule_files entry pointing to /etc/prometheus/recording_rules.yml (which you will create in Task 2). The evaluation_interval must be set to 15s. Confirm that both targets appear as UP in the Prometheus targets UI at http://<instance-ip>:9090/targets before moving on.

sudo tee /etc/prometheus/prometheus.yml <<'EOF'
global:
  scrape_interval:     15s
  evaluation_interval: 15s

rule_files:
  - "/etc/prometheus/recording_rules.yml"

scrape_configs:
  - job_name: prometheus
    static_configs:
      - targets: ["localhost:9090"]

  - job_name: node
    static_configs:
      - targets: ["localhost:9100"]
EOF

sudo chown prometheus:prometheus /etc/prometheus/prometheus.yml

# Validate the configuration before reloading
/opt/prometheus/promtool check config /etc/prometheus/prometheus.yml

# Reload Prometheus (the --web.enable-lifecycle flag makes this endpoint available)
curl -fsSL -X POST http://localhost:9090/-/reload
